---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import { site } from '../data/project';

const updated = '25 October 2026';
---

<Marketing title="Privacy policy · Outflare" description="What Outflare collects on this website and in the hosted app at app.outflare.ai, how Google user data is used, and how to have your data deleted.">
	<section class="relative border-b">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
			<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
			<h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tighter text-balance sm:text-5xl">Privacy policy</h1>
			<p class="sub">Last updated {updated}.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
		<div class="legal">
			<p>
				This policy covers the website at outflare.ai and the hosted app at app.outflare.ai (together, "Outflare", "we"). If you run Outflare on your own server, your data stays on that server and we never see it; the only thing a self-hosted server sends us is the{' '}
				<a href="/docs/self-hosting/telemetry/">anonymous daily report</a>, which you can turn off.
			</p>

			<h2>The website</h2>
			<p>outflare.ai is a static site. It sets no cookies, runs no advertising or tracking scripts, and has no accounts. Our host, Cloudflare, keeps standard request logs (such as IP address and browser) for security and reliability.</p>

			<h2>What the hosted app collects</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Your account:</strong> name, email address, a hashed password or passkey, and, if you use Continue with Google, your Google account's email, name and ID.</li>
				<li><strong>What you put in:</strong> mailboxes you connect (with their credentials, encrypted at rest), leads, sequences, emails sent and replies received, and settings.</li>
				<li><strong>Connected tools:</strong> the data you choose to read in from connectors such as Google Analytics, Search Console or a calendar.</li>
				<li><strong>Usage and logs:</strong> sign-in times, IP address, and a daily count of what each workspace used, so we can keep the service running and fair.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>How we use it</h2>
			<p>Only to run the service you asked for: sign you in, send and receive the email you set up, show your reports, keep the service secure, and contact you about your account. We do not sell personal data, use it for advertising, or train AI models on it.</p>

			<h2>Google user data</h2>
			<p>When you connect a Google account, Outflare asks only for what that feature needs:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Sign-in</strong> (openid, email, profile): to identify you and link your Outflare account.</li>
				<li><strong>Gmail</strong>: to send the email in your sequences from your mailbox and to read replies to them, so they appear in your Outflare inbox.</li>
				<li><strong>Google Analytics and Search Console</strong> (read-only): to show your site's traffic and search performance in your workspace.</li>
				<li><strong>Google Calendar</strong> (events, read-only): to count meetings booked from your outreach.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Outflare's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
				<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Google data is used only to provide those features to you, is never sold, never used for advertising, and never used to train AI models. People at Outflare do not read it unless you ask us to for support, it is needed for security, or the law requires it.
			</p>
			<p>You can disconnect a Google account in Outflare at any time, and revoke access from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google account permissions</a>.</p>

			<h2>Who processes it for us</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Railway</strong> hosts the app and its database in the United States.</li>
				<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website and our DNS.</li>
				<li><strong>Our account-email provider</strong> sends confirmation and password reset emails.</li>
				<li><strong>Providers you connect</strong>, such as Google, Microsoft or a mailbox supplier, receive what's needed for the action you take, under their own terms.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Keeping and deleting data</h2>
			<p>We keep your data while your account is open. Delete a workspace or ask us to close your account and we delete its data within 30 days, except what we must keep by law. Encrypted backups roll off within a further 30 days.</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>You can ask to see, correct, export or delete your personal data. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we'll reply within 30 days.</p>

			<h2>Security</h2>
			<p>Traffic is encrypted in transit, mailbox credentials and OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest, and access is limited to the people who run the service. To report a vulnerability, see our <a href="/docs/project/security/">security policy</a>.</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll update the date above and tell account holders by email before it takes effect.</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Marketing>
